# a [[righteye flounder]] {{gl|[[flatfish]] of the family {{taxfmt|Pleuronectidae|family}}}}
#* {{RQ:Wamyō Ruijushō|8|passage=王餘魚 朱厓記云：南海有<sub>二</sub>王餘魚<sub>一</sub>［和名：加良衣比、俗<sub>二</sub>云：'''加禮比'''<sub>一</sub>］昔、越王作<sub>レ</sub>[[鱠]]不<sub>レ</sub>盡餘半棄<sub>レ</sub>水因以<sub>二</sub>半身<sub>一</sub>爲<sub>レ</sub>魚、故曰<sub>二</sub>王餘魚<sub>一</sub>也|translation=Righteye flounder {{qlit|king-remaining fish}}: according to the ''Zhūyá'' chronicle, at the southern sea there exists a righteye flounder (Japanese name ''kara-ei'', commonly said '''''karei'''''); long ago, the king of Yuè had not completely made [[kuai#Etymology 1|kuài]] and discarded half of the remaining into the water; as a result half of his body turned into a fish, hence the name.}}
# {{lb|ja|sort=かれい|rare|obsolete}} {{synonym of|ja|舌鮃|tr=shitabirame}}: a [[sole#Etymology 2|sole]] {{gl|flatfish of the family {{taxfmt|Soleidae|family}}}}

