===Etymology===
{{ja-kanjitab|わに|yomi=k}}

From {{inh|ja|ojp|-|sort=わに}}. Ultimate derivation uncertain.

In the ''{{w|Kojiki}}'', {{m|ja|わに}} refers ambiguously to a sea creature, interpreted either as a [[shark]] or a [[crocodile]]. The sense “crocodile” is explicit in the ''{{w|Wamyō Ruijushō}}'' (938), which describes it as a four-legged, turtle-like animal with a long mouth and sharp teeth.

Proposed etymologies include comparison with Proto-Tai *ŋɨək / *ŋɨːk (“saltwater crocodile; mythical sea monster”), as argued by Vovin, and derivation from an early borrowing of Sinitic {{m|zh|黿}}, possibly influenced semantically by {{m|zh|鼉}} (“crocodile; alligator”).

